  CVE-2026-35535|2026-04-03T03:16:18.233|2026-04-03T16:10:23.730|7.4|HIGH|CWE-271|N/A|false|In Sudo through 1.9.17p2 before 3e474c2, a failure of a setuid, setgid, or setgroups call, during a privilege drop before running the mailer, is not a fatal error and can lead to privilege escalation.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-35535|0.00004|0.00183|5.1801
  CVE-2026-28815|2026-04-03T03:16:18.093|2026-04-03T16:10:23.730|7.5|HIGH|CWE-125|N/A|false|A remote attacker can supply a short X-Wing HPKE encapsulated key and trigger an out-of-bounds read in the C decapsulation path, potentially causing a crash or memory disclosure depending on runtime protections. This issue is fixed in swift-crypto version 4.3.1.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-28815|0.00017|0.03971|5.2505
