  CVE-2024-44303|2026-04-02T19:18:38.960|2026-04-03T16:10:23.730|7.5|HIGH|CWE-284|N/A|false|The issue was addressed with improved checks. This issue is fixed in macOS Sequoia 15.1. A malicious application may be able to modify protected parts of the file system.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-44303|0.00081|0.24089|5.2524
  CVE-2024-44286|2026-04-02T19:18:36.140|2026-04-03T16:10:23.730|7.5|HIGH|CWE-288|N/A|false|This issue was addressed through improved state management. This issue is fixed in macOS Sequoia 15.1. An attacker with physical access can input keyboard events to apps running on a locked device.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-44286|0.00097|0.26864|5.2529
